    "confidence": "HIGH for the 38 ships below. Every value was read off a live in-game card, not a fan wiki.",
    "structure": "6 classes x 7 rates. Rate VII is the smallest/weakest, rate I the largest. Class determines role: Fast=speed, Battle/Combat=weapons, Transport=hold, Heavy=defense, Siege=mortars, Imperial=special.",
    "criticalFields": {
      "hold": "The ONLY cargo constraint. There is NO separate cargo-slot limit - this was an early design assumption that proved false. Hold is measured in the same units as item weight (1:1).",
      "speed": "BASE speed only. In game the HUD displays a RANGE (e.g. Pickle 9.2-11.7) where the first number is base and the second is max cruise speed. Cards show only the base. The calculator uses BASE and must visibly note that actual speed varies with wind direction, sail upgrades and cargo load.",
      "rate": "Integer 1-7, converted from the Roman numeral shown in game. Governs shallow-water access: a port with 'Shallow waters ranks VI-7' admits ONLY rate 6 and 7 ships, for BOTH docking and undocking.",
      "upgradeSlots": "Observed to vary by ship (e.g. Pickle 6, Russia 8). Where unknown, null. The Structural Expansion upgrade adds +2."
    },
    "validationEvidence": "Live in-game ship HUDs confirmed that upgrade modifiers apply correctly on top of these base values: Le Cerf base hold 8000 -> live 11000 (+3000 Double Hold) and base durability 900 -> live 855 (-5% Double Hold). Russia base 22000 -> live 26500 (+3000 Double Hold +1500 Cellars) and 1600 -> 1520 (-5%). Horizont base durability 850 -> live 930 (+80 Repair Arsenal). The flat/percentage modifier model is therefore verified against real data.",
    "incompleteRoster": "The Fandom wiki lists ~58 ships total. The 38 below are those visible in the user's shipyard plus one premium ship. NOT YET CAPTURED: Axel Thorsen, Svannah, Sovereign, Le Saint Louis, Kwee Song, Shunsen, Flying Cloud, Friedrich Wilhelm, St. Pavel, Vasa, Azov, Shen, Firestorm, Neptuno, De Zeven Provincien, Santisima Trinidad, Prins Willem, Red Arrow, Sparrow, Eagle. Individual wiki pages exist for each; they can be added without new screenshots. The app must handle an incomplete roster gracefully and allow users to add ships."
